/** @page ncursesreleasenotes Release Notes

    @section ncurses_1_0 ncurses Module Version 1.0
    - initial release

    Scrollable text prepares wrapping before measuring scroll limits, maps
    source positions to display cells, preserves the viewport anchor on resize,
    and clips styled Unicode text at widget boundaries. Cursor requests can be
    released without disturbing a newer request from another widget. Develop
    pipelines reuse successful platform tests for identical Git trees.

    Focus routing reaches nested controls, modal scopes preserve Tab traversal
    and restore eligible prior focus, and explicit popups support outside-click
    dismissal. Text inputs and combo boxes share grapheme-safe editing and mouse
    caret mapping. Cursor indices remain character offsets; partial replacement
    ranges expand to whole graphemes. Session::setCursor() now returns the prior
    visibility so modal transitions can restore it exactly. Composite file-browser
    pane navigation stays synchronized with managed focus, and combo-box mouse
    placement and dropdown scrolling share the clipped drawing geometry.
    Composite mouse delegation preserves preview navigation. Focus callbacks share a thread-local transition guard,
    including cleanup triggered by hiding, disabling, and detaching widgets.
    Modal initialization rolls back if a focus callback makes its root
    unavailable, and file-browser keyboard delegation excludes unavailable panes.
    Outside primary clicks, including double and triple clicks, close menu panels
    and release menu state before forwarding the event to the underlying control.

    Panel children now share the screen-coordinate layout/input contract and
    convert drawing to window-local coordinates. Clipped inputs keep the caret
    visible at the right edge; panel windows accept focused child cursor requests.
    Derived native windows retain their parents, preventing shared-storage leaks
    when the parent wrapper is released first. Panel replacement preserves the
    old resources on creation failure. Box layouts constrain overflowing requests,
    and active dialogs and anchored popups reflow on resize. Tiny dialogs expose
    every action through keyboard navigation and scroll wrapped messages.

    Tables add stable identity across refreshes, numeric/date/string/custom
    sorting, filtering, horizontal column navigation, row actions, primary mouse
    selection, double-click activation and wheel navigation. Equal sort keys are
    stable; invalid data/comparator failures preserve the preceding view.
    Radio groups, menus and combo boxes keep active choices visible using actual
    drawable rows, support page/home/end and mouse navigation, and clear obsolete
    rows. Disabled-only menus no longer risk an unbounded navigation loop.
    Nested panels retain logical geometry and open intent independently of clipped
    native resources, including full clipping and later regrowth. Hit testing
    follows ancestor clipping; left-clipped lists, checkboxes, menus and status
    bars render their visible suffixes. Table column selection stays visible after
    resize, and empty row hashes remain valid selections for actions and activation.

    TextEditorWidget adds hard newlines, soft wrapping, styled prompts, preferred
    visual columns, bounded height, selection, clipboard hooks, undo/redo and
    searchable history that restores unfinished drafts. Bracketed paste arrives
    as a bounded Paste event, with fragmented input, cancellation and oversized
    payload recovery. Native and injected Alt input preserve Unicode characters.
    Synthetic event batches now commit atomically into a bounded module queue;
    overflow leaves previously queued input intact.

    TranscriptWidget adds stable source identities, logical blocks, incremental
    streaming updates, retention, search/highlights, selection/copy, collapse and
    link callbacks. Manual scrolling pauses following and tracks unread output.
    Indexed line extents and two cached wrap widths avoid rewrapping old text on
    appends/edits. InputBuffer caches grapheme positions. Dirty drawing preserves
    overlapping siblings, exposed regions and modal overlays while skipping idle
    frames. Width-aware box measurement sizes wrapped editors before allocation.

    qrepl uses separate transcript and draft viewports, retains failed drafts,
    exposes output/history search and internal clipboard bindings, and anchors
    completion to the wrapped caret. Ordinary Enter is normalized without changing
    literal paste or Alt input. Clipped subtree invalidation, clean panel removal,
    transcript mouse anchors, scrollbar following and collapse source text are covered
    by regressions. Its capture worker uses explicit flush and
    shutdown acknowledgement, preserves blank lines and split UTF-8, and reports
    invalid output bytes without sending malformed strings to the renderer.
*/
